# Content delivery architecture (pointer)

Full law: [`docs/docs/architecture/content-delivery.md`](../../docs/docs/architecture/content-delivery.md).

**Permanent decision:** three surfaces, never conflated. **Build Web** ships
project files (scenes, prefabs, planets, systems, referenced/allowlisted
assets). **Postgres catalog** (ships, props, items, weapons, backpacks,
wearables, game settings, commerce, mob defs/packs when live, mission
defs/boards when live) is edited **per environment** via Server
Console `/admin/*`. **Migrations** are schema + one-shot seeds only — not
continuous catalog sync. Prod `RUN_MIGRATIONS` defaults off unless set. Editor
Play reads the live project; a shipped build uses the bundle — local success
does not prove release completeness.

When changing catalog promote paths, Build Web asset copy, Server Console
definitions, or “works in Play / fails on play host” asset bugs, read the full
doc first. Also listed in `AGENTS.md`.
